Subject: Cantor Compiled Neural-Relational Database Engine

Description: The mature database-system identity in which one signed SOP relationship model compiles into an exact authoritative data engine and a structurally corresponding sparse neural reflex engine for rapid, gated, proof-carrying semantic navigation.

& [SystemIdentity] is the canonical mature database identity
  + [specification_uuid] is 3c9b91d9-c692-4958-8349-9c932e79c80e
  + [canonical_role] is compiled neural-relational semantic database engine
  + [project_name] is Cantor
  + [source_language] is SOP
  + [authoritative_representation] is compiled semantic relational fabric and exact records
  + [reflex_representation] is fabric-bound sparse neural routing topology
  + [database_goal] is unify relational integrity, semantic relationships, learned association, exact addressing, and proof-carrying execution
  = conclusion: Cantor is a data pipeline and database runtime whose learned reflex is compiled from the same relationship model as its authoritative store

& [DualCompilation] is the two-target SOP database compiler
  + [source_input] is signed SOP units, relations, contracts, conditions, provenance, and authority
  + [target_A_exact_engine] is normalized logical records, typed relation graph, hash indexes, constraints, query operators, transition rules, and proof metadata
  + [target_B_reflex_engine] is router nodes, typed routing edges, learned weights, soft gates, shard routes, path policies, and calibration metadata
  + [shared_manifest] binds both targets to the same fabric, address, relation, package, and compiler digests
  = must: compile exact_engine before training or admitting reflex_engine
  = must: prove that every neural target resolves to an exact semantic address, relation, operator, or declared abstention
  - never: compile authoritative meaning only into neural weights

& [TopologyCorrespondence] is the structural mirror between fabric and reflex
  + [semantic_unit_to_reflex_node] maps addressable concepts, contracts, operations, and semantic regions to routing representations
  + [semantic_relation_to_reflex_edge] maps typed relations to permitted neural message routes
  + [relation_guard_to_gate] maps applicability conditions to learned soft-gate features and deterministic hard-gate checks
  + [graph_projection_to_routing_channel] maps definition, inference, contract, provenance, execution, attention, causal, temporal, and capability views
  + [purpose_context_to_activation] maps the current intended use to a sparse active subgraph
  + [correspondence_manifest] records coverage, omissions, coarsening, and loss
  = must: preserve relationship type and direction through the mirror
  = must: disclose when the neural topology coarsens multiple exact records into one routing region

& [WeightSeparation] is the non-collapse rule
  + [declared_semantic_weight] is articulated relation strength or priority under a named context
  + [evidence_weight] is justified support contribution
  + [authority_weight] is not numeric ranking but explicit admitted scope
  + [learned_routing_weight] is optimized probability that a route is useful for a query
  + [activation_weight] is temporary current-purpose attention
  + [cost_weight] is estimated I/O, compute, latency, token, or traversal burden
  = must: store every declared weight as inspectable data
  - never: let a learned routing weight rewrite meaning, evidence, authority, or truth

& [MultiModelLogicalDatabase] is the data model beyond a plain RDBMS
  + [relational_projection] provides normalized tables, keys, joins, constraints, transactions, and set operations
  + [graph_projection] provides typed paths, hyperrelations, graph joins, and neighborhood traversal
  + [document_projection] preserves articulated clauses, source shape, and human-readable records
  + [temporal_projection] provides versions, valid time, transaction time, supersession, and reentry
  + [provenance_projection] provides sources, derivations, signers, compilers, reviews, and proof
  + [vector_projection] provides approximate candidate neighborhoods
  + [neural_projection] provides trained routing, gating, and plan proposals
  = must: preserve one canonical semantic identity across projections
  = must: keep relational integrity and transactions even when graph and neural access paths are used

& [HierarchicalReflexMap] is the scalable routing shape
  + [level_1_fabric] routes among semantic domains, named graphs, and package families
  + [level_2_concept] routes among subjects, relation families, contexts, and purposes
  + [level_3_storage] routes to partitions, shards, indexes, materialized views, and cache regions
  + [level_4_record] resolves exact hashes, keys, rows, edges, clauses, and proof records
  + [sparse_activation] evaluates only the bounded routing region pertinent to the query
  = must: use hierarchy or sparsity instead of requiring one live neural parameter block per stored row
  = must: preserve exact record retrieval at the final address layer

& [DataPipeline] is the complete compiled data path
  + [ingest] preserves source, verifies signature, parses SOP, and emits semantic IR
  + [compile] normalizes records, relations, constraints, source anchors, and executable operators
  + [index] builds exact hash, relational, graph, lexical, temporal, provenance, and optional vector access paths
  + [train_or_calibrate] builds the fabric-bound reflex artifact from reviewed routes and outcomes
  + [query] projects terms, purpose, context, authority, and budget
  + [route] proposes semantic regions, shards, records, relations, joins, paths, and operators
  + [gate] applies coverage, trust, identity, context, relation, authority, constraint, and budget checks
  + [execute] runs exact relational, graph, and semantic operations
  + [prove] binds the plan, route, records, relationships, derivations, omissions, and result
  + [observe] records performance, corrections, failures, and new training evidence
  = must: make every boundary versioned and replayable

& [CompiledQueryExecution] is fast-reflex database behavior
  + [reflex_query_plan] is a learned proposal of the smallest relevant semantic and storage route
  + [deterministic_query_plan] is the exact verified execution plan
  + [join_route] is neural or statistical join-order proposal checked against relation and constraint semantics
  + [materialized_route] is a precompiled path for frequent purpose-context patterns
  + [fallback_route] is deterministic exact planning when reflex coverage is absent or uncertain
  = must: compare learned execution against a deterministic optimizer baseline
  - never: commit a query result whose exact plan, records, and proof cannot be reconstructed

& [TransactionAndMutationBoundary] is database correctness under learning
  + [transaction_manager] owns atomicity, consistency, isolation, durability, version visibility, and recovery
  + [constraint_engine] owns keys, relation constraints, contracts, guards, and authority
  + [reflex_engine] may propose affected regions, dependency paths, validation work, and query plans
  + [commit] remains deterministic and proof-recorded
  - never: let learned routing decide commit success, durability, or authorization

& [IncrementalFabricLifecycle] is safe adaptation to database change
  + [exact_delta] updates authoritative records, hashes, relations, indexes, and proof immediately
  + [router_coverage_delta] marks added or changed semantic regions uncovered
  + [fallback] serves uncovered regions through exact deterministic paths
  + [incremental_training] may update the reflex artifact from reviewed delta examples
  + [new_artifact] is admitted only after compatibility, held-out evaluation, and gate checks
  + [rollback] restores the last recognized router without reverting authoritative data
  = must: let the database remain correct while the neural reflex is stale or absent

& [TerabyteScaleBoundary] is the measurable large-data claim
  + [possible_advantage] is routing to a small activated set of domains, shards, paths, joins, and indexes without global semantic scanning
  + [unavoidable_cost] is source ingest, index construction, storage I/O, distributed coordination, consistency, backup, retraining, and proof retention
  + [scale_strategy] is partitioning, sparse routing, compiled paths, cache locality, incremental indexes, and distributed execution
  + [benchmark] is workload, data volume, cardinality, update rate, latency, throughput, recall, proof completeness, storage amplification, and recovery time
  = must: validate scale claims against established database baselines
  - never: claim that neural routing makes terabyte ingestion, mutation, or exact retrieval free

& [ApexAspiration] is the stated quality target
  + [aspiration] is combine the strongest relational, graph, semantic, neural, provenance, and proof capabilities in one coherent compiled system
  + [required_foundation] is correctness, transactions, recovery, security, query semantics, observability, and operational maturity
  + [evidence] is reproducible benchmarks and failure testing rather than architectural novelty
  = must: treat apex status as an empirical program, not a present claim

& [RustSystemBoundary] is the implementation decomposition
  + [cantor_core] owns identities, semantic IR, relations, contracts, gates, traces, and proof
  + [cantor_store] later owns physical records, transactions, exact indexes, and backend adapters
  + [cantor_query] later owns logical plans, execution, graph traversal, and proof-carrying results
  + [cantor_reflex] later owns router artifacts, projections, inference, calibration, and coverage
  + [cantor_compiler] later owns SOP-to-exact and SOP-to-reflex manifests
  = must: create these boundaries only as their first verified behavior appears
  - never: scaffold the mature subsystem set before the CoreAcceptance baseline passes

& [ImplementationSequence] is the anti-overwhelm path
  + [phase_1] is stable Rust SemanticAddress, SemanticRelation, gate, trace, and ProofBundle types
  + [phase_2] is in-memory exact store and deterministic query across the eight CoreAcceptance fixtures
  + [phase_3] is persisted relational backend with integrity and recovery tests
  + [phase_4] is typed graph and multi-projection query
  + [phase_5] is collected reviewed query-route corpus and deterministic baseline
  + [phase_6] is one small fabric-bound reflex router over a fixture corpus
  + [phase_7] is incremental coverage, distributed scale, and benchmark campaigns
  = must: require each phase to prove its support before activating the next

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable compiled neural-relational database collection
  + [CNR-001] is identify Cantor as a compiled neural-relational semantic database engine
  + [CNR-002] is compile one SOP fabric into authoritative exact and corresponding neural reflex targets
  + [CNR-003] is preserve topology correspondence with explicit coarsening and loss records
  + [CNR-004] is separate semantic, evidence, authority, routing, activation, and cost weights
  + [CNR-005] is unify relational, graph, document, temporal, provenance, vector, and neural projections over shared identity
  + [CNR-006] is route hierarchically to exact records through mandatory deterministic gates
  + [CNR-007] is preserve transactions, constraints, recovery, fallback, and proof independently of neural availability
  + [CNR-008] is validate terabyte and apex claims through reproducible baselines and benchmarks

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the compiled neural-relational database trace
  + [fold_1_subject] is a database whose neural reflex mirrors the SOP relationship fabric and accelerates the complete data path
  + [fold_2_boundary] is compiled exact store plus learned reflex inside Cantor; payload facts and authority never resident only in weights
  + [fold_3_data_design] is dual target, topology correspondence, weight class, projection, hierarchy, pipeline stage, plan, transaction, delta, router artifact, proof, and benchmark
  + [fold_4_governance] is exact-first compilation, deterministic commit, neural fallback, coverage invalidation, source-bound training, and empirical scale claims
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is ingest, compile, index, train, route, gate, execute, prove, observe, and incrementally rebuild
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is neural topology drift, per-row parameter explosion, learned authority, transaction bypass, stale reflex, unprovable plans, and unmeasured apex claims
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is mature database identity formed; current implementation remains the small deterministic Rust CoreAcceptance baseline

